        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಕೂಡಲೇ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕೂಡಲೇ — kūḍalē — \"at once; immediately\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಸುದ್ದಿ ಕೇಳಿದ ಕೂಡಲೇ ಅಜ್ಜ ಆಸ್ಪತ್ರೆಗೆ ಹೊರಟರು. suddi kēḷida kūḍalē ajja āspatrege horaṭaru. As soon as he heard the news, Grandfather set off for the hospital."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "After a past form it means \"as soon as\": ಕೇಳಿದ ಕೂಡಲೇ (kūḍalē), as soon as (he) heard."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕೂಡಲೇ (kūḍalē) is built on the native Dravidian verb kūḍu, \"to join, to meet\" (DEDR 1882), with the emphatic ending -ē; how it came to mean \"at once\" is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
